From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:19:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] Red team fix 3: the index releases its per-file notes
 when it is cleared

The notes of the loaded index files (pack IDs and blob counts, used by the
index rewrite) were kept when the index was cleared and loaded again, so a
long-lived process that sees index files replaced (mount --no-lock beside a
prune) kept one note for every index file it had ever loaded. clear now
releases them; the files loaded afterwards are noted again. Rewrite decides
which files it keeps before it clears the index, from the same notes as
before.

Test (seat 2 finding 5, carried in): TestIndexNotesReleasedOnReload fails
before this commit (100 notes for one live file) and passes after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
